 "desc": "Goal: Learn MIPS arithmetic and bitwise operations. add and sub work on three registers (destination, source1, source2). sll (shift left logical) multiplies by powers of 2 — sll $t4, $t0, 2 is the same as $t0 * 4. srl (shift right logical) divides by powers of 2. These shifts are critical in MIPS — the compiler uses them constantly instead of multiply instructions.",
 "source": [
  "# MIPS Arithmetic & Shifts",
  "# $t0 = 15, $t1 = 7 (preloaded)",
  "",
  "add $t2, $t0, $t1   # $t2 = 15 + 7",
  "sub $t3, $t0, $t1   # $t3 = 15 - 7",
  "sll $t4, $t0, 2     # $t4 = 15 << 2 (x4)",
  "srl $t5, $t1, 1     # $t5 = 7 >> 1  (/2)",
  "and $t6, $t0, $t1   # $t6 = 15 & 7",
  "or  $t7, $t0, $t1   # $t7 = 15 | 7",
  "hlt"
 ],
